sys_lwcond: lv2 layout (u32 lwmutex EA at +0, u32 queue id at +4) and real wait/signal with the
lv2 timeout and ETIMEDOUT. KZ3 FIOS reads +0 and spun on "wait for invalid cond" with the old 64-bit store.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): partly absorbed, layout from PR277 same offsets, per-waiter wait/signal kept.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): #577 replaced the lwmutex semaphore with a state word: the lwcond wait releases/retakes through `lwm_release`/`lwm_acquire`, `ppu_thread_note_block` kept (1059 and 1122 then replace it).

